Exception', 'description': "If the RRset's name is not a subdomain of the zone's origin, addRRset should throw an IllegalArgumentException."}]}, {'group': 'addRRset(RRset) - Different types same name', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rrset', 'value': 'RRset{name=host.example.com., type=A, records=[ARecord 192.0.2.1 TTL=3600] }'}], 'expected': 'findExactMatch(host.example.com., A) returns the A RRset; findExactMatch(host.example.com., AAAA) later returns the AAAA RRset.', 'description': 'Adding two RRsets with the same owner name but different types should store both independently.'}]}, {'group': 'addRRset(RRset) - Adding SOA record', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rrset', 'value': 'RRset{name=example.com., type=SOA, records=[SOARecord mname=ns1.example.com. rname=hostmaster.example.com. serial=2023101501 refresh=7200 retry=3600 expire=1209600 minimum=3600 TTL=3600] }'}], 'expected': 'getSOA() returns the added SOARecord', 'description': "Adding an SOA RRset for the zone origin should set the zone's SOA record, accessible via getSOA()."}]}, {'group': 'addRRset(RRset) - Adding NS record', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rrset', 'value': 'RRset{name=example.com., type=NS, records=[NSRecord ns1.example.com. TTL=3600, NSRecord ns2.example.com. TTL=3600] }'}], 'expected': 'getNS() returns the NS RRset containing both NS records', 'description': 'Adding an NS RRset for the zone origin should be stored and returned by getNS().'}]}, {'group': 'addRRset(RRset) - Large RRset', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rrset', 'value': 'RRset{name=big.example.com., type=A, records=[ARecord 10.0.0.1 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.2 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.3 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.4 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.5 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.6 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.7 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.8 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.9 TTL=300, ARecord 10.0.0.10 TTL=300] }'}], 'expected': 'findExactMatch(big.example.com., A) returns RRset with 10 A records; no exception is thrown.', 'description': 'The m